WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.416 --> 00:00:03.997
Every Sunday for eleven years, Tom sat in the last pew.

2
00:00:03.997 --> 00:00:08.294
He came in after the opening hymn and left during the closing one.

3
00:00:08.294 --> 00:00:10.313
He never went up for Communion.

4
00:00:10.313 --> 00:00:13.568
He never shook anyone's hand at the sign of peace,

5
00:00:13.568 --> 00:00:16.368
because there was never anyone near enough.

6
00:00:16.818 --> 00:00:18.511
Frank, the usher, noticed.

7
00:00:18.511 --> 00:00:20.139
Frank noticed everything.

8
00:00:20.139 --> 00:00:24.631
One Sunday, instead of standing at the back, he sat down next to Tom.

9
00:00:25.081 --> 00:00:25.993
Tom stiffened.

10
00:00:25.993 --> 00:00:28.467
"I'm not much of a Catholic," he said.

11
00:00:28.917 --> 00:00:31.782
"Neither was the tax collector," Frank said.

12
00:00:31.782 --> 00:00:33.475
"He stood at the back too.

13
00:00:33.475 --> 00:00:37.121
Jesus said he was the one who went home right with God."

14
00:00:37.571 --> 00:00:38.743
Tom didn't answer.

15
00:00:38.743 --> 00:00:43.105
But at the sign of peace, Frank held out his hand, and Tom took it.

16
00:00:43.555 --> 00:00:46.876
The next week, Tom came in during the opening hymn.

17
00:00:47.326 --> 00:00:50.777
The week after that, he sat three rows from the back.

18
00:00:50.777 --> 00:00:53.837
And the week after that, he went to confession.

19
00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:56.696
It started with someone sitting down.
